<title>USA: Kaiser Aluminum abandons recapitalization.</title>
<headline>Kaiser Aluminum abandons recapitalization.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kaiser Aluminum Corp said directors abandoned a proposed recapitalization of the company that would have allowed for the creation of two classes of common stock.</p>
<p>The company said the board's decision follows the Delaware Supreme Court's decision upholding a Chancery Court preliminary injunction blocking the proposal.</p>
<p>In conjunction with the board action, Kaiser said, the company filed a motion to dismiss the shareholder litigation.</p>
<p>It said the decision to withdraw the proposal does not preclude a recapitalization from being proposed to stockholders in the future, including a substantially identical structure after the redemption or conversion of the company's preferred convertible stock.</p>
<p>Kaiser Aluminum is about 62 percent owned by MAXXAM Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
